      "consensus": "0.5%",
      "previous": "-0.4%",
      "description": "Retail Sales measure the change in the total value of inflation-adjusted sales at the retail level. It is the foremost indicator of consumer spending, which accounts for the majority of overall economic activity.\r\n&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;A higher than expected reading should be taken as positive/bullish for the NZD, while a lower than expected reading should be taken as negative/bearish for the NZD."
